  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), F-15E/EX throttle handle unit without base, seen from the side; one end face (right on the photo) carries a ribbed gray knob, a cone 5-way hat, a black knurled thumb wheel and a gray lever; knurled ring and mounting pin at the other end (left)",
  "mappingSource": "catalog source only: EDCD EliteCustomButtonNames device map 4098BD64 (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EDCD/EliteCustomButtonNames/main/files/INTO%20Bindings/DeviceButtonMaps/4098BD64.buttonMap): Handle L = Small Button Right 50, Back Hat 51-55, Small Button Left 56, Side Lever 57-59, Rotary Rz + UP/MID/DOWN 60-62. No WinWing manual for the StrikeAce handles found (en.winwing.cn/en/download lists only firmware F15EX_HANDLE_L / F15_HANDLE_R), so which physical control is which name is not documented",
  "confidence": "low",
  "note": "Only the cone hat is placed (the map has one 5-way hat on handle L, the \"Back Hat\"); the knob, wheel and lever are kept as hidden candidates because the side lever / rotary / small-button names cannot be matched to them without a vendor drawing. The two small buttons are not identifiable on this photo. Catalog issue: this handle entry also carries the whole Orion 2 throttle BASE (switches/encoders/buttons 65-111, Slider = SLIDER1 and Dial = SLIDER2 levers) from the EDCD whole-device map; those are on the base, not on this handle, so they are marked not on this photo.",
